WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.241
MAN: Aah!

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:09.109
[phone rings]

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.311
SIMON: Guys! Guys! Crew!

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:13.346
It might be a callout!

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:15.348
[phone rings]

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:17.117
Hello, hello?

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:19.119
Yes, I can hear you.

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:20.153
You have a snake?

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.488
Okay, calm down, it's okay.

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:22.922
What color?

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:25.125
Yeah, what, black?

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:26.926
Gray?

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.728
Okay, you can't see all of it.
Okay, well, don't go near it.

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.597
Can you get someone just
to stand there and watch it?

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:32.031
Very important.

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:34.167
Do not move away from there,
and just get them to watch it.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.803
And we'll be on our way, yes,
we'll come now, right now, yes.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.872
Do me a favor,
SMS me your address,

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:41.107
it'll make things
quicker for us, too, okay.

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:42.942
And don't leave the snake, okay?

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:44.677
We're coming now,
okay, bye, bye.

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:46.112
Right, guys,
it's a possible callout.

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:47.480
He says it's big and it's black,

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:49.616
and he only saw half of it,
and it's gone outside.

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:50.784
So, we're going to need
to move it up.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:51.618
Okay, ready?

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:56.156
♪ ♪

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:58.458
♪ Poison ♪

00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:00.326
I'm Simon Keys.

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:02.896
That's my girlfriend,
Siouxsie Gillett.

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:05.265
We're professional
snake catchers.

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:08.601
For $30, you get rid
of an unwanted visitor,

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:12.372
we get to save a snake's life.

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:14.073
SIOUXSIE: I would never
change what I do. I love it.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:17.076
SIMON: Our passion is to keep
the snakes alive.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.512
♪ Poison, poison, poison ♪

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:28.388
Hello? Are you alright?

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:29.722
Got to you in the end,
alright, guys,

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:31.291
how are you, how are you,
Simon, how are you doing?

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:32.659
Simon and Siouxsie, alright.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:33.893
Okay.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:34.928
SIOUXSIE: Hey, I'm sorry
for the day, I'm Siouxsie.

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:35.962
Hi, pleased to meet you.

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:36.863
SIMON: Alright.
Nice to meet you.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.031
SIOUXSIE: Oh, hello!

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:39.332
SIMON: Okay, get the little...
Go, go, doggie.

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:43.036
SIOUXSIE: Oh, okay.
SIMON: Oh, okay, right.

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:43.970
MAN: So I moved the car,
it's right...

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:45.004
SIMON: In those bricks?

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:46.539
Okay. And you say black?

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.441
MAN: It's black, like,
it just stood like this.

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:50.477
SIMON: Stood up.
Shiny back, or like a...?

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:51.578
MAN: Shiny.
SIMON: Okay.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:52.879
MAN: Shiny black, yes.

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:53.980
SIMON: Alright, get the little
doggie out of here.

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:54.848
I'll tell you why,
if it bites the dog,

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:57.283
the dog's, the dog's history.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:00.753
If it is,
if it is what we think it is.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.989
I'll tell you what,
let's switch these glasses.

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:05.091
Give me some yellows.

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:07.594
When people say black snake
in this city,

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.230
it's most likely to be
one of five dark snakes,

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:13.366
and I need to be prepared
for any one of those.

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:16.970
One, a house snake,
or two, a herald snake,

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.638
both harmless to humans.

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:21.174
Three, a Mozambique
spitting cobra,

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:23.776
highly venomous and it can spit
its venom accurately

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:26.613
at your eyes from six feet away.

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:29.516
Four, a forest cobra.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.518
It can't spit, but it has
a much more potent

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:35.154
and fast-acting neurotoxic venom
than the spitting cobra.

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:38.391
Or five, a black mamba.

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:42.729
A fast snake and a venomous bite
that can kill you in 30 minutes.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:45.665
Did you see it in the middle bit
here, or this bit?

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:50.503
SIMON: Right.
Whoa, it's a lot of bricks.

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:53.907
Maybe best you just stand back,
just in case it's a mamba.

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:55.341
MAN: Yeah, because...

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:56.876
SIMON: Or the cobra,
it'll be fast.

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:58.511
SIOUXSIE: Have you pretty much
kept your eye on it,

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:00.580
that you know it's,
it hasn't come out, basically?

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:04.250
SIMON: Siouxsie's an experienced
snake handler,

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:06.853
but this is her first season
catching wild snakes.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.588
SIOUXSIE: It'll be a case
of moving the brick.

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:09.889
I keep thinking my mum
is going to kill me

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:11.157
if she found out what I'm doing.

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:12.859
She thinks I'm sort of relaxing
and reading on the beach

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:15.862
while Simon's out here
working and catching snakes.

00:03:15.929 --> 00:03:17.564
SIMON: It's really important
to Siouxsie, you know,

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.032
to get a grip with this
very quickly,

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:20.967
because, let's say something
goes wrong.

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:23.570
Say I get bitten,
and that snake's still loose,

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:24.637
she's got to catch it.

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:25.738
Can't just leave it.

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:30.577
We have to move,
it's about 400 bricks.

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:32.111
This is gonna take, you know...

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:32.946
SIOUXSIE: A while.

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.847
SIMON: Half an hour.

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:36.749
Well, basically,
it's gone behind here,

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:38.451
and obviously we can't pull it
out from the bottom.

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:40.720
We've got to go from the top
and work our way down.

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:42.889
So it's going to take time.

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:44.891
Hopefully the snake's behind
there, curled up somewhere.

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:48.795
A bit dodgy, because you can end
up getting a bite on the finger,

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:52.131
so I'm just doing little bit
by little bit.

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:54.300
You know, I don't want
to get bitten.

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:57.003
So, ooh, you see, geckos.

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:58.838
Anything that moves.

00:04:03.242 --> 00:04:04.277
Have you got a bit here?

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:05.612
SIOUXSIE:
Just want to check this gap.

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:07.146
SIMON: My mind is racing.

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:09.749
It's a hot day today,
so whatever snake is in here

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:12.719
is going to be charged up
and ready to strike.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:15.288
A black mamba could shoot out
and bite me on my legs,

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:17.123
a spitting cobra could
nail me in the eyes

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.424
before I even see it.

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:19.892
Okay.

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:21.227
Lots of eyes are
better than two,

00:04:21.294 --> 00:04:24.831
so just watch me legs,
nothing comes shooting out.

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:29.769
SIOUXSIE: If it's that big,
that's what I'm thinking.

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:32.338
SIMON: If it is something
like a mamba or cobra,

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:33.606
all hell could break loose,

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:35.341
so just bear in mind
we might have to jump back,

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:37.710
these bricks might go flying.

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:40.013
So, now I'm going to pile bricks
there and on top of there,

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:41.280
so now I've got a clear exit
out there.

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:42.582
SIOUXSIE: You don't want
to brick yourself in, no.

00:04:42.649 --> 00:04:45.952
SIMON: No, no. So, just in case.

00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:49.122
I'm hoping to be see,
see behind here soon.

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:50.323
SIOUXSIE: There's a gap there,
can you see it?

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.325
SIMON: There is a little bit
of a gap there.

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:57.964
You ready with that grabber
if I call you?

00:04:58.031 --> 00:05:00.233
SIOUXSIE: Ooh, I can see it!
There we go, a head.

00:05:00.299 --> 00:05:01.367
SIMON: Where?
SIOUXSIE: There.

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:02.201
SIMON: Yep.
SIOUXSIE: Cobra.

00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:03.870
SIMON: Forest cobra. Okay.

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:06.272
The forest cobra is the biggest
cobra in Africa,

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:08.574
reaching over eight feet
in length.

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:12.812
It's an alert and nervous snake,
therefore dangerous.

00:05:14.514 --> 00:05:16.449
The fast-acting neurotoxic venom

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:18.351
attacks the central
nervous system,

00:05:18.418 --> 00:05:21.254
paralyzing the muscles
that control breathing.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:23.890
Untreated, you could be dead
within hours.

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:24.724
It's here.

00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:27.794
Um, one glove, left. Ta.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:31.130
Right, I need to,
I'm going to push these off.

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:36.436
I've got a feeling it might
get under the wall here.

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:40.273
Where are you going,
where are you going?

00:05:40.339 --> 00:05:42.775
It's going to come out
this side, I think, so.

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:54.020
Where's your head?

00:05:54.087 --> 00:05:58.391
Which end have I...
I think I've got the tail.

00:05:58.458 --> 00:06:00.226
Just going to pull a little bit.

00:06:00.293 --> 00:06:01.627
Right.

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:03.096
SIOUXSIE: Can I get in
with my hand to do the bricks?

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:04.230
SIMON: No, no,
don't touch the...

00:06:04.297 --> 00:06:06.132
SIOUXSIE: No, no, no,
with the glove.

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:07.734
SIMON: Just get that brick there
out the way.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.135
Okay, he's not going
anywhere now.

00:06:09.202 --> 00:06:10.670
SIOUXSIE: So I can move
the brick with my hand?

00:06:10.737 --> 00:06:12.038
SIMON: No, no,
not with your hand.

00:06:12.105 --> 00:06:15.608
I've got the tail end, yeah,
put, yeah, use that hand.

00:06:15.675 --> 00:06:18.711
I have kind of thrown Siouxsie
right in the deep end,

00:06:18.778 --> 00:06:20.880
and she's probably thinking,
Christ, what's going on?

00:06:20.947 --> 00:06:22.248
There's a lot going
through my head now,

00:06:22.315 --> 00:06:24.684
I've got to pass him this,
grab that, put a glove on,

00:06:24.751 --> 00:06:27.086
grab the tongs, grab the hook,
put the goggles on.

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:28.755
You know, it's like chaos.

00:06:28.821 --> 00:06:29.989
SIOUXSIE: I do just hope
I'm quick enough

00:06:30.056 --> 00:06:32.325
just to make sure
nothing happens to him.

00:06:32.391 --> 00:06:34.594
I think in that situation
it is life or death.

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:35.928
SIMON: Lift that brick
up if you can.

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:37.964
Just, in you go. Oh, he's going.

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:39.766
I can't grip with these things.

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:40.767
Watch my leg.

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:42.635
SIOUXSIE: Yeah.
SIMON: Okay, that'll do.

00:06:42.702 --> 00:06:45.238
SIMON: Right, it's coming out.

00:06:45.304 --> 00:06:46.973
Okay, forest cobra.

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:48.241
[sighs]

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:50.109
Right, can you take these
glasses off my face?

00:06:50.176 --> 00:06:51.310
I can't see what I'm doing.

00:06:51.377 --> 00:06:54.046
Thank you. Right,
don't need them anymore.

00:06:54.113 --> 00:06:55.348
Alright, that's a forest cobra.

00:06:55.414 --> 00:06:57.950
It's probably about a year,
a year and a bit old,

00:06:58.017 --> 00:07:01.154
year and a half old,
not much more than that.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:03.322
These ones can't spit.

00:07:03.389 --> 00:07:07.026
Just give me the other glove
on there for a second.

00:07:07.093 --> 00:07:08.561
SIOUXSIE: Here?
SIMON: Yeah, yeah.

00:07:08.628 --> 00:07:10.029
SIMON: Very dangerous snake,

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:13.533
neurotoxic venom,
that'll cause paralysis.

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:15.434
Serious stuff.

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:17.904
If he bites my finger,
it doesn't matter, I hope.

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:20.640
If you look at the tail there,

00:07:20.706 --> 00:07:22.275
you see it's got quite a point
on the end of it?

00:07:22.341 --> 00:07:23.643
SIOUXSIE: Oh, that's
the defense, isn't it?

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:24.610
SIMON: That's the defense.

00:07:24.677 --> 00:07:26.379
So when I've got him like this,

00:07:26.445 --> 00:07:28.381
he'll actually stick that tail
into my skin,

00:07:28.447 --> 00:07:31.017
and people that are unaware
of that would actually drop it,

00:07:31.083 --> 00:07:33.085
thinking they'd been bitten,
it's quite sharp.

00:07:33.152 --> 00:07:34.086
SIOUXSIE: He's doing it now,
isn't he?

00:07:34.153 --> 00:07:35.121
SIMON: Yeah,
he's doing it now.

00:07:35.188 --> 00:07:36.589
It doesn't actually
break the skin.

00:07:36.656 --> 00:07:38.057
But if you didn't know
about the snake,

00:07:38.124 --> 00:07:39.292
you'd probably think
you've just been bitten,

00:07:39.358 --> 00:07:40.793
if you grabbed it
willy-nilly, you know.

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:42.228
I think he's feeling
fairly relaxed now.

00:07:42.295 --> 00:07:43.062
SIOUXSIE:
Yeah, he's quite calm.

00:07:43.129 --> 00:07:44.263
SIMON: He's not too bad.

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:46.199
Like I say, you treat each one
individually.

00:07:46.265 --> 00:07:48.434
I've caught some psychos, yeah,
he might have a go at my finger.

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:49.669
SIOUXSIE: Might have a bite now.
Look at that.

00:07:49.735 --> 00:07:51.070
Do you trust those gloves?
That's what I'm saying.

00:07:51.137 --> 00:07:52.338
SIMON: Only one way
to find out.

00:07:52.405 --> 00:07:53.573
It should be alright.

00:07:53.639 --> 00:07:54.841
SIOUXSIE: No, we don't want
to risk it, do we?

00:07:54.907 --> 00:07:56.242
SIMON: So you guys,
you're scared of the snake?

00:07:56.309 --> 00:07:57.543
MAN: Yeah.

00:08:00.279 --> 00:08:01.881
SIMON: Yeah, it is
a dangerous snake.

00:08:01.948 --> 00:08:03.015
No problem.

00:08:03.082 --> 00:08:05.151
I think we need to get this
into a bag.

00:08:05.218 --> 00:08:06.786
Maybe just put the towel
in between those two fingers.

00:08:06.853 --> 00:08:08.154
SIOUXSIE: Mm-hmm.

00:08:08.221 --> 00:08:09.622
SIMON: Now, what I'm going
to do, I'm going to put that...

00:08:09.689 --> 00:08:11.090
No, no, no, no, no. Go on, then.

00:08:11.157 --> 00:08:13.426
You've got a little bite there,
don't bite yourself, though.

00:08:13.492 --> 00:08:14.994
Come here. He's having a go
on the glove.

00:08:15.061 --> 00:08:16.262
SIOUXSIE: You want to keep him
off the glove?

00:08:16.329 --> 00:08:18.431
SIMON: No, it's alright.
Oh, yeah, you really feel that.

00:08:18.497 --> 00:08:19.265
SIOUXSIE: I hope it works.

00:08:19.332 --> 00:08:20.299
SIMON: Okay, let go of him.

00:08:20.366 --> 00:08:21.667
He'll be, yeah, better
to just let go.

00:08:21.734 --> 00:08:24.570
Yeah, you can really feel
the pressure on the glove there

00:08:24.637 --> 00:08:26.405
when they bite.

00:08:26.472 --> 00:08:28.040
It's not a particularly pleasant
feeling,

00:08:28.107 --> 00:08:29.742
I can be honest with you.

00:08:29.809 --> 00:08:32.511
If that was your, if that was
on my skin now, bare skin,

00:08:32.578 --> 00:08:34.614
I'd really be in big trouble.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:35.815
SIMON: Push him into the bag.
SIOUXSIE: Right.

00:08:35.882 --> 00:08:37.350
SIMON: You let go of the bag,
quickly.

00:08:37.416 --> 00:08:38.184
Now he's in the bag.

00:08:38.251 --> 00:08:39.518
SIOUXSIE: I'll get tape.

00:08:39.585 --> 00:08:40.753
SIMON: Yeah, get the tape.
Push it all the way down.

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:41.988
Got gloves on,
so it's not dangerous.

00:08:42.054 --> 00:08:43.256
SIOUXSIE: Watch your belly.

00:08:43.322 --> 00:08:44.857
SIMON: Yeah, keep it away
from the old belly.

00:08:44.924 --> 00:08:46.259
Twist, twist, twist,
all the way to the top.

00:08:46.325 --> 00:08:49.028
Snake's right there,
can't do anything.

00:08:49.095 --> 00:08:50.696
That's it, the snake's
in the bag.

00:08:50.763 --> 00:08:51.864
Don't go near the bag.

00:08:51.931 --> 00:08:53.299
The snake will bite you
through the bag.

00:08:53.366 --> 00:08:54.133
SIOUXSIE: Now put all
the bricks back.

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:56.569
SIMON: And we'll...

00:08:56.636 --> 00:08:57.703
Oh, yeah, no. That's their job.

00:08:57.770 --> 00:08:59.205
SIOUXSIE: Help.
[laughs]

00:08:59.272 --> 00:09:00.339
SIMON: I'll let them do that,
I think.

00:09:00.406 --> 00:09:02.708
I've done my building course
for one day.

00:09:02.775 --> 00:09:04.110
SIMON: Thanks, man.
MAN: Thanks, guys.

00:09:04.176 --> 00:09:05.945
MAN: Thank you very much for
your help, thank you, thank you.

00:09:06.012 --> 00:09:07.413
SIMON: No worries.
SIOUXSIE: No problem at all.

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:09.048
SIOUXSIE: Thank you very much.
Thank you. No, you take care.

00:09:09.115 --> 00:09:12.285
Thank you, bye, take care!

00:09:15.588 --> 00:09:17.256
SIMON: Just about all
of Africa's deadliest

00:09:17.323 --> 00:09:19.158
and most dangerous snakes
are found here,

00:09:19.225 --> 00:09:21.694
in Durban, South Africa.

00:09:21.761 --> 00:09:23.696
Every day we drive for miles
across the city,

00:09:23.763 --> 00:09:24.964
catching problem snakes

00:09:25.031 --> 00:09:27.366
and releasing them
into nature reserves and bush,

00:09:27.433 --> 00:09:29.936
in and around the city.

00:09:30.002 --> 00:09:31.671
But today is different.

00:09:31.737 --> 00:09:36.042
Our next callout is only
a few doors down.

00:09:36.108 --> 00:09:38.945
We just got in the car and,
like, literally 30 seconds,

00:09:39.011 --> 00:09:42.081
the security guy comes
screaming down the road

00:09:42.148 --> 00:09:43.816
saying there's another big snake

00:09:43.883 --> 00:09:45.418
just literally a minute
around the corner.

00:09:45.484 --> 00:09:46.452
I thought he was just
having a joke,

00:09:46.519 --> 00:09:47.586
you know, a bit of a laugh.

00:09:47.653 --> 00:09:48.587
Can you believe that?

00:09:48.654 --> 00:09:51.290
What the hell is
going on here today?

00:09:51.357 --> 00:09:52.992
When your morning
starts out like this,

00:09:53.059 --> 00:09:57.129
you know each callout is going
to get even crazier and crazier.

00:09:57.196 --> 00:10:00.866
I had no idea how big and bad
today would get.

00:10:00.933 --> 00:10:03.436
Crazy stuff.

00:10:03.502 --> 00:10:05.504
When it goes, when it starts
happening, it starts happening.

00:10:05.571 --> 00:10:06.939
You don't stop, you know.

00:10:07.006 --> 00:10:10.343
Like, just grab stuff.
Okay. Here we go.

00:10:15.381 --> 00:10:17.416
SIOUXSIE:
Oh, he's locked me in.

00:10:19.518 --> 00:10:20.686
SIMON: Around the side?
MAN: Yeah.

00:10:20.753 --> 00:10:22.054
SIMON: What color?

00:10:28.594 --> 00:10:31.797
SIMON: Oh, yeah.
Another forest, quick!

00:10:31.864 --> 00:10:33.733
It's getting away!

00:10:36.335 --> 00:10:37.503
Where's it gone?

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:39.538
SIOUXSIE: I'm here,
I'm here with the gloves.

00:10:39.605 --> 00:10:40.573
I can't see where you are.

00:10:40.639 --> 00:10:41.841
SIMON: Sioux, quick!

00:10:41.907 --> 00:10:43.843
SIOUXSIE:
I'll go the other way.

00:10:47.613 --> 00:10:48.914
SIMON: Sioux,
he's coming your way.

00:10:48.981 --> 00:10:50.649
SIOUXSIE: Whoa, whoa,
I can't see!

00:10:50.716 --> 00:10:52.051
SIMON: Grab some tongs.

00:10:52.118 --> 00:10:53.786
Watch out!
It's by your legs, guys.

00:10:53.853 --> 00:10:55.287
Watch, it's coming out,
it's coming out.

00:10:55.354 --> 00:10:56.589
SIOUXSIE: Where are you?
I can see where you are.

00:10:56.655 --> 00:10:58.491
SIMON: There, there,
there, there.

00:10:58.557 --> 00:10:59.325
Run in there.

00:11:06.399 --> 00:11:07.466
SIOUXSIE: Run in there.
Okay, let me get grabbers.

00:11:07.533 --> 00:11:08.667
SIMON: The forest cobra
has the upper hand,

00:11:08.734 --> 00:11:10.403
you know, in the bushes,
in the trees.

00:11:10.469 --> 00:11:13.839
So you see it for a second
and then it disappears.

00:11:13.906 --> 00:11:15.174
Where's it, where's it?

00:11:15.241 --> 00:11:17.410
Right, watch there. Sioux?

00:11:17.476 --> 00:11:18.244
SIOUXSIE: I'm here
getting tools.

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:19.478
SIMON: Grab tongs?

00:11:19.545 --> 00:11:20.312
SIOUXSIE: I'm getting tools,
I'm getting tools.

00:11:20.379 --> 00:11:22.681
SIMON: Stay there. Went in here.

00:11:22.748 --> 00:11:23.949
SIOUXSIE:
I've got no bag ready.

00:11:24.016 --> 00:11:26.652
SIMON: It's gone in the bloody
tree, I missed it.

00:11:28.687 --> 00:11:29.455
SIOUXSIE: Could you not
leave it here?

00:11:29.522 --> 00:11:30.956
Is it not happy in this natural?

00:11:31.023 --> 00:11:32.124
SIMON: No.

00:11:32.191 --> 00:11:33.692
SIOUXSIE: Oh, it's someone's
garden. Okay.

00:11:33.759 --> 00:11:36.829
SIMON: Yeah, I've just missed it
by a half a centimeter,

00:11:36.896 --> 00:11:38.731
and now it's in here.

00:11:38.798 --> 00:11:40.866
Right, can you watch that side?

00:11:40.933 --> 00:11:42.368
SIOUXSIE:
We haven't got anything?

00:11:42.435 --> 00:11:44.503
SIMON: No, you stay that side.
SIOUXSIE: Yeah.

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:48.507
SIMON: And I need someone.
Can you stay by the gate?

00:11:48.574 --> 00:11:50.976
And just look up that
back section there.

00:11:51.043 --> 00:11:52.745
So if he comes out,
then you can just shout,

00:11:52.812 --> 00:11:54.980
and I'll try and get to it.

00:11:59.118 --> 00:12:02.088
And also, look up
in the tree as well.

00:12:02.154 --> 00:12:03.956
They climb super fast.

00:12:04.023 --> 00:12:05.391
That just went past your leg,

00:12:05.458 --> 00:12:09.161
right about missed you
by about two inches.

00:12:09.228 --> 00:12:11.330
Close.

00:12:11.397 --> 00:12:13.866
SIOUXSIE: Definitely
a forest, yeah?

00:12:13.933 --> 00:12:16.235
SIMON: Yeah, yeah.
Do you not see it?

00:12:16.302 --> 00:12:17.636
SIOUXSIE: I didn't see it.

00:12:17.703 --> 00:12:19.805
I was running around getting
tubs and snakes and bags and...

00:12:19.872 --> 00:12:20.806
SIMON: It was moving so fast,

00:12:20.873 --> 00:12:22.308
but I just missed it
with the tongs.

00:12:22.374 --> 00:12:23.375
And you know what?

00:12:23.442 --> 00:12:25.344
It'll climb up this thing
so easy.

00:12:29.548 --> 00:12:30.616
SIOUXSIE: This snake
can do anything.

00:12:30.683 --> 00:12:32.785
It can climb,
it can stay on the ground,

00:12:32.852 --> 00:12:34.320
but there is huge piles
of leaves,

00:12:34.386 --> 00:12:38.424
so, for us, nature is
against us, with camouflage.

00:12:38.491 --> 00:12:41.760
So it's hidden away.

00:12:41.827 --> 00:12:43.095
So now it's just a case
of literally digging through

00:12:43.162 --> 00:12:44.497
all these leaves
trying to find it.

00:12:44.563 --> 00:12:46.799
SIMON: Alright, can you look
in the tree?

00:12:46.866 --> 00:12:48.200
Just keep looking
up into the tree.

00:12:48.267 --> 00:12:50.069
SIOUXSIE: So, now Simon's
telling me to keep looking up,

00:12:50.136 --> 00:12:51.203
when obviously
we've looked already

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:53.172
around the ground,
dug through the leaves.

00:12:53.239 --> 00:12:54.773
The key thing here is now,
I mean,

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:56.742
it literally is look everywhere,
up and down.

00:12:56.809 --> 00:12:58.144
SIMON: It's in here somewhere,
but I don't know.

00:12:58.210 --> 00:12:59.512
There's so much bush.

00:12:59.578 --> 00:13:00.346
SIOUXSIE: And they're fast,
so it doesn't help us.

00:13:00.412 --> 00:13:01.180
It's probably already...

00:13:01.247 --> 00:13:02.214
SIMON: Watch your legs, guys.

00:13:02.281 --> 00:13:03.382
This thing shot,
literally, in seconds.

00:13:03.449 --> 00:13:04.850
SIOUXSIE: Do you want me
to go the other side?

00:13:04.917 --> 00:13:07.286
SIMON: Go the other side, just
keep looking up in the trees.

00:13:07.353 --> 00:13:09.221
You'll see it for a second,
then it disappears.

00:13:09.288 --> 00:13:11.857
And the first time it was going
along the floor, just whoosh,

00:13:11.924 --> 00:13:13.826
fast, fast, fast,
head up, moving around,

00:13:13.893 --> 00:13:15.194
zipping along
like nobody's business.

00:13:15.261 --> 00:13:16.962
Trying to get away, obviously.

00:13:17.029 --> 00:13:18.397
I don't want to lose it,
so I'm running after it,

00:13:18.464 --> 00:13:20.432
and I'm tripping
over twigs and branches,

00:13:20.499 --> 00:13:21.700
hitting myself in the head,

00:13:21.767 --> 00:13:23.969
you know, it's like, and as I go
to put the tongs on it,

00:13:24.036 --> 00:13:25.171
I missed it by about an inch.

00:13:25.237 --> 00:13:26.739
You know, a tiny amount
like that.

00:13:26.805 --> 00:13:29.074
I thought, oh,
and then he's off.

00:13:32.344 --> 00:13:34.346
The guy that we just did
the previous callout

00:13:34.413 --> 00:13:36.982
with the bricks, he decided
to walk around the corner

00:13:37.049 --> 00:13:39.885
to, you know, come and have
a look with his mate.

00:13:41.587 --> 00:13:43.489
SIMON: Where, where, where?

00:13:43.556 --> 00:13:46.725
Okay, keep an eye on it.

00:13:46.792 --> 00:13:48.394
SIOUXSIE: This guy is good.

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:49.828
SIMON: Oh, yeah,
it's up the tree.

00:13:49.895 --> 00:13:51.163
Okay, hold that.

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:52.398
SIOUXSIE: Where, where, where?

00:13:52.464 --> 00:13:53.666
SIMON: Going up.

00:13:53.732 --> 00:13:56.669
Keep an eye on it all the time,
until I get up the tree.

00:13:56.735 --> 00:13:59.138
Hold that one sec.
Quick, quick, quick.

00:13:59.205 --> 00:14:00.172
He's going that way.

00:14:00.239 --> 00:14:01.006
SIOUXSIE: What are you
going to do?

00:14:01.073 --> 00:14:02.408
SIMON: I don't know.

00:14:02.474 --> 00:14:04.310
SIOUXSIE: Do you need a tool
up there? Tool and gloves?

00:14:04.376 --> 00:14:06.545
I've got it, really high up.
What do you want, gloves?

00:14:06.612 --> 00:14:08.414
SIMON: Give me the tongs.

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:11.750
Where is it now? Oh, yeah,
he's going to the other tree.

00:14:11.817 --> 00:14:14.353
Just watch, don't take
your eyes off it.

00:14:14.420 --> 00:14:18.724
[heavy breathing]

00:14:18.791 --> 00:14:19.825
How can I get over there?

00:14:19.892 --> 00:14:20.759
SIOUXSIE: What are
your plans, Simon?

00:14:20.826 --> 00:14:21.760
Do you want me to be somewhere?

00:14:21.827 --> 00:14:23.662
SIMON: I don't know.
Catch snake.

00:14:23.729 --> 00:14:25.698
Just keep watching it.

00:14:25.764 --> 00:14:27.933
Forest cobras are
excellent climbers.

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:29.702
Instead of the typical
serpentine movement

00:14:29.768 --> 00:14:31.470
of the lateral S-bends,

00:14:31.537 --> 00:14:34.673
they also use a concertina-like
movement in the trees.

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:35.808
They contract muscles that pull

00:14:35.874 --> 00:14:38.110
its specialized belly scales
forward,

00:14:38.177 --> 00:14:41.413
the back edge of these scales
catching on the bark.

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:43.716
Using other muscles,
it then pushes these scales

00:14:43.782 --> 00:14:47.086
against the bark, propelling
the whole body forward.

00:14:47.152 --> 00:14:49.588
Ooh, he's going faster
than I can go.

00:14:49.655 --> 00:14:50.422
SIOUXSIE: Where's it going?

00:14:50.489 --> 00:14:53.058
SIMON: Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh.

00:14:53.125 --> 00:14:55.327
Ah, he's in the tree here,
I missed him again.

00:14:55.394 --> 00:14:56.595
Look, just keep looking there.

00:14:56.662 --> 00:14:57.429
SIOUXSIE: I've got him,
I've got him, I can see him.

00:14:57.496 --> 00:14:58.831
SIMON: Where is it?

00:14:58.897 --> 00:14:59.965
SIOUXSIE: Right, it's just
in the gap between the trees,

00:15:00.032 --> 00:15:02.434
the two dead bits of leaves
at the top.

00:15:02.501 --> 00:15:03.636
He's going to cross now.

00:15:03.702 --> 00:15:07.139
He's literally, his tail's
going in that gap.

00:15:07.206 --> 00:15:08.274
SIMON: Where?

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:09.475
SIOUXSIE: Right, see that bunch
of dead leaves,

00:15:09.541 --> 00:15:11.010
opposite that bit.

00:15:11.076 --> 00:15:11.844
SIMON: I can't see it.

00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:13.045
SIOUXSIE: You can't see it?

00:15:13.112 --> 00:15:14.446
Now I've lost him,
he's gone in that, though,

00:15:14.513 --> 00:15:16.282
all that collection
of dead leaves,

00:15:16.348 --> 00:15:18.984
opposite the bit you're in.

00:15:19.051 --> 00:15:19.852
He's gone in there.

00:15:19.918 --> 00:15:21.153
SIMON: In there?
SIOUXSIE: Yeah.

00:15:21.220 --> 00:15:22.888
SIMON: Bugger!

00:15:22.955 --> 00:15:25.324
There's nothing else
to stand on here.

00:15:25.391 --> 00:15:27.359
Venom from the bite
of a forest cobra

00:15:27.426 --> 00:15:29.828
moves through the human body
much faster

00:15:29.895 --> 00:15:32.765
than many other species
of venomous snake.

00:15:32.831 --> 00:15:34.066
The attack on the nervous system

00:15:34.133 --> 00:15:36.468
may affect muscle control
in minutes,

00:15:36.535 --> 00:15:39.672
not something you want
15 feet up in a tree.

00:15:39.738 --> 00:15:40.739
SIOUXSIE: Can you shake it?

00:15:40.806 --> 00:15:43.175
SIMON: No, because
I could fall out.

00:15:43.242 --> 00:15:44.677
Alright, I missed again.

00:15:44.743 --> 00:15:45.911
SIOUXSIE: Watching Simon
up the tree

00:15:45.978 --> 00:15:48.347
trying to catch the cobra,
it's very hard to watch,

00:15:48.414 --> 00:15:50.349
and I think, you know, it is
like watching your partner

00:15:50.416 --> 00:15:52.084
have a gun held to their head.

00:15:52.151 --> 00:15:55.254
It's a very serious situation.

00:15:55.321 --> 00:15:58.324
I don't think that looks safe.

00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:00.659
SIMON: Watch my head.

00:16:00.726 --> 00:16:02.928
[branches breaking]
Oh, fricking hell.

00:16:02.995 --> 00:16:04.697
SIOUXSIE: Can you grab?
SIMON: Oh.

00:16:04.763 --> 00:16:06.665
SIOUXSIE:
Right, are you alright?

00:16:06.732 --> 00:16:08.133
SIMON: It wasn't going well
for me.

00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:09.435
No, not at all.

00:16:09.501 --> 00:16:10.269
Siouxsie?

00:16:10.336 --> 00:16:11.970
SIOUXSIE: I'm here.

00:16:12.037 --> 00:16:13.405
What are you doing?

00:16:13.472 --> 00:16:15.140
SIMON: I've got a grab on it,
but it's in the wrong spot.

00:16:15.207 --> 00:16:17.409
I'm in the top of the tree now,
and I've got the snake,

00:16:17.476 --> 00:16:19.078
and I've got to make a decision.

00:16:19.144 --> 00:16:20.913
I've got the cobra in one hand
with the tongs,

00:16:20.979 --> 00:16:21.914
I'm holding on with the other.

00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:23.215
The branches are very thin,

00:16:23.282 --> 00:16:24.550
they're bending and tipping
all over the place.

00:16:24.616 --> 00:16:26.151
I can't get a very good grip.

00:16:26.218 --> 00:16:28.420
So I'm thinking maybe I will
just pass it to Siouxsie,

00:16:28.487 --> 00:16:29.922
she can deal with it.

00:16:29.988 --> 00:16:32.057
I don't know if that was
the right thing to do or what.

00:16:32.124 --> 00:16:33.992
You know, sorry, darling,
you know, here,

00:16:34.059 --> 00:16:37.096
just deal with this
meter-long forest cobra.

00:16:37.162 --> 00:16:39.398
SIMON: Whoa, whoa, whoa!
It's going again.

00:16:39.465 --> 00:16:41.033
SIOUXSIE: Where we going?
Where we going? I can't see.

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:42.334
SIMON: It's falling down!
SIOUXSIE: Down, down, down.

00:16:42.401 --> 00:16:43.535
SIMON: Sioux, there, quick!

00:16:43.602 --> 00:16:50.843
SIOUXSIE: I can't,
I'm too short, too short!

00:16:50.909 --> 00:16:52.444
SIOUXSIE: Watch your leg!
Watch your leg!

00:16:52.511 --> 00:16:54.613
SIMON: Where'd it go?

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:56.281
There, it's on the floor! Quick!

00:16:56.348 --> 00:16:58.684
Just grab it anywhere, anywhere.
Have you got it?

00:16:58.751 --> 00:16:59.718
SIOUXSIE: Not yet, not yet.

00:16:59.785 --> 00:17:01.887
SIMON: Quick, quick,
quick, quick!

00:17:01.954 --> 00:17:03.355
SIOUXSIE: Oh, blast it.

00:17:03.422 --> 00:17:04.356
SIMON: The fricking thing.

00:17:04.423 --> 00:17:05.357
SIOUXSIE:
I got--no, it's going.

00:17:05.424 --> 00:17:07.259
SIMON: Where's it gone?
Have you got it?

00:17:07.326 --> 00:17:08.360
SIOUXSIE: I've got the tail
and that's it.

00:17:08.427 --> 00:17:09.862
SIMON: Just hold it down,
I'm coming.

00:17:09.928 --> 00:17:11.230
Coming down, guys,
I'm gonna jump down.

00:17:11.296 --> 00:17:12.398
SIOUXSIE: I don't know
where it's gone.

00:17:12.464 --> 00:17:14.767
I can't see, I've got the tip
of the tail.

00:17:14.833 --> 00:17:16.835
Down there, down there.

00:17:16.902 --> 00:17:18.670
Oh, yeah, I've got a bit of it.

00:17:18.737 --> 00:17:19.705
Watch yourself, watch yourself.

00:17:19.772 --> 00:17:21.607
SIMON: Where'd it go?

00:17:21.673 --> 00:17:23.675
Not again!

00:17:23.742 --> 00:17:25.544
SIOUXSIE: This thing
is bloody good.

00:17:25.611 --> 00:17:27.112
SIMON: Damn.

00:17:27.179 --> 00:17:30.048
Now where's it gone?

00:17:30.115 --> 00:17:31.150
Damn the thing.

00:17:31.216 --> 00:17:32.818
Stay there.

00:17:34.219 --> 00:17:36.121
Bastard.

00:17:39.792 --> 00:17:41.860
SIOUXSIE: There was a time
at one point I saw it come down

00:17:41.927 --> 00:17:43.662
and actually get
next to Simon's ankle.

00:17:43.729 --> 00:17:45.531
I actually did think he bit him
at one point,

00:17:45.597 --> 00:17:48.667
from the angle I could see,
it was very, very close.

00:17:48.734 --> 00:17:50.636
Um, and you know, you do,

00:17:50.702 --> 00:17:52.771
it's, you know,
your natural human emotion

00:17:52.838 --> 00:17:55.808
is that it's, your loved one's
up a tree

00:17:55.874 --> 00:17:57.643
being potentially bitten
by a cobra.

00:17:57.709 --> 00:18:00.813
That's a really awful,
awful situation to be in.

00:18:00.879 --> 00:18:02.114
SIMON: Yeah, I was a bit
concerned about that,

00:18:02.181 --> 00:18:04.349
to be honest with you.

00:18:04.416 --> 00:18:06.485
SIMON: Well, I've missed it
three times.

00:18:06.552 --> 00:18:08.887
The snake has got the upper hand
here, because they're so agile.

00:18:08.954 --> 00:18:12.357
I think it's gone deep
into that palm tree there.

00:18:12.424 --> 00:18:14.226
I think if I don't dig it out
in the next couple minutes,

00:18:14.293 --> 00:18:16.495
we'll have to just
leave it here.

00:18:19.932 --> 00:18:22.234
SIOUXSIE: In the middle,
literally.

00:18:22.301 --> 00:18:23.669
SIMON: Where?

00:18:23.735 --> 00:18:25.237
SIOUXSIE: Where, where, where?
SIMON: Where, where, where?

00:18:25.304 --> 00:18:26.505
SIMON: Where?

00:18:26.572 --> 00:18:28.273
MAN: There, there, right by you.
SIMON: Where is it?

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:29.174
SIOUXSIE: Right--oh!

00:18:29.241 --> 00:18:30.876
SIOUXSIE: There.
SIMON: Where?

00:18:30.943 --> 00:18:32.044
SIOUXSIE: Bloody leaves!

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:34.179
I've got some of it.
Have you got it?

00:18:34.246 --> 00:18:35.113
SIMON: Yep.

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:36.448
Right, glove, please.

00:18:36.515 --> 00:18:37.649
SIOUXSIE: Here! Left hand?
SIMON: Left hand, quickly!

00:18:37.716 --> 00:18:38.851
SIOUXSIE: Left hand.

00:18:38.917 --> 00:18:40.252
SIMON: I've got right hand.

00:18:40.319 --> 00:18:43.121
SIOUXSIE: You want right hand?

00:18:43.188 --> 00:18:46.558
SIMON: Right hand.
SIOUXSIE: Right hand, go.

00:18:46.625 --> 00:18:48.660
SIMON: Left hand.
SIOUXSIE: Go, go.

00:18:48.727 --> 00:18:52.731
SIMON: Watch out, left hand.
SIOUXSIE: Yep.

00:18:52.798 --> 00:18:55.467
SIMON: Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:18:55.534 --> 00:18:57.002
Let's get out here a bit,
let me just...

00:18:57.069 --> 00:18:58.370
SIOUXSIE: Can you grab it a bit?

00:18:58.437 --> 00:19:02.007
SIMON: You little bugger,
oh, gave me the run around.

00:19:02.074 --> 00:19:04.943
Let him settle down
for a minute.

00:19:05.010 --> 00:19:06.078
There we just go like that.

00:19:06.144 --> 00:19:07.379
Hey, hey, hey, hey.

00:19:07.446 --> 00:19:09.448
Hey, hey, oh, oh, oh.

00:19:09.515 --> 00:19:10.616
Thank you.

00:19:10.682 --> 00:19:11.984
SIOUXSIE: There we go.
SIMON: There we go.

00:19:12.050 --> 00:19:13.652
SIOUXSIE: That was good.

00:19:13.719 --> 00:19:14.920
SIMON: Oh, you're cheeky.

00:19:14.987 --> 00:19:17.256
Both of us nearly had you
twice, three times.

00:19:17.322 --> 00:19:18.290
He's having a good bite there.

00:19:18.357 --> 00:19:20.125
SIOUXSIE: Where's your
right hook?

00:19:20.192 --> 00:19:21.126
Just in case we don't...

00:19:21.193 --> 00:19:22.294
SIMON: No, he's alright,
he's just...

00:19:22.361 --> 00:19:23.161
SIOUXSIE: I just don't trust
these gloves.

00:19:23.228 --> 00:19:24.396
SIMON: No, they're alright.

00:19:24.463 --> 00:19:26.265
Yeah, they can zip
through those trees so well.

00:19:26.331 --> 00:19:27.232
You can't see them.

00:19:27.299 --> 00:19:29.301
SIOUXSIE: Twice now!
MAN: Yeah.

00:19:29.368 --> 00:19:31.203
SIMON: Twice in ten minutes.

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:32.204
An hour.

00:19:32.271 --> 00:19:34.339
Twice in an hour.

00:19:34.406 --> 00:19:35.574
Crazy.

00:19:35.641 --> 00:19:37.876
A little bit smaller than
the other one, I think.

00:19:37.943 --> 00:19:39.545
Yeah, a little bit smaller.

00:19:39.611 --> 00:19:40.879
Just as dangerous, though.

00:19:40.946 --> 00:19:42.080
Crazy.

00:19:42.147 --> 00:19:44.850
Come on, let go, let go.

00:19:50.689 --> 00:19:51.957
No, it's holding on.

00:19:52.024 --> 00:19:54.192
Okay, this is a forest cobra.

00:19:54.259 --> 00:19:58.030
A bit smaller than the previous
one, just as dangerous,

00:19:58.096 --> 00:20:01.300
and very agile on the floor
and the trees.

00:20:01.366 --> 00:20:03.135
So, it's terrestrial
and arboreal.

00:20:03.201 --> 00:20:05.337
And it glides
through those trees

00:20:05.404 --> 00:20:07.573
way faster than I could climb
up and down.

00:20:07.639 --> 00:20:10.475
A couple of times I nearly fell
out, hanging on with one hand.

00:20:10.542 --> 00:20:12.110
I pinned it behind the head,

00:20:12.177 --> 00:20:13.378
didn't have a glove
on the other hand.

00:20:13.445 --> 00:20:16.782
I just going to,
do I grab it with my hand?

00:20:16.848 --> 00:20:18.483
I just wasn't feeling
comfortable with it,

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:21.286
I was losing the grip anyway.

00:20:21.353 --> 00:20:23.021
Then it got away again,
then it went down,

00:20:23.088 --> 00:20:26.224
then Sioux managed to grab it
by the tail,

00:20:26.291 --> 00:20:27.459
and it still managed
to slip through.

00:20:27.526 --> 00:20:28.594
That's the problem
with these gloves,

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:29.828
although they might save you
from a bite,

00:20:29.895 --> 00:20:31.930
you don't get a good grip.

00:20:31.997 --> 00:20:34.066
You can check, like,
the underneath.

00:20:34.132 --> 00:20:36.234
SIOUXSIE: So here we've got
the belly scales here.

00:20:36.301 --> 00:20:39.104
If you see how they lift, that
is actually how they grip on,

00:20:39.171 --> 00:20:42.107
that's how they're able to climb
trees, purely because of this.

00:20:42.174 --> 00:20:43.508
Oh, the tail got me there,
made me jump.

00:20:43.575 --> 00:20:44.843
SIMON: Yeah, see.

00:20:44.910 --> 00:20:47.012
SIOUXSIE: Yeah, see,
that's the defense, it works.

00:20:47.079 --> 00:20:48.447
SIMON: It's like
a scorpion tail there.

00:20:48.513 --> 00:20:49.681
SIOUXSIE: So, yeah, so he's
digging me with the tail there,

00:20:49.748 --> 00:20:50.983
that's the defense.

00:20:51.049 --> 00:20:52.250
You can see it's a real sharp
point on the end there,

00:20:52.317 --> 00:20:53.385
and that's the bit, as I say,
is their defense.

00:20:53.452 --> 00:20:54.386
You think you're being bitten,

00:20:54.453 --> 00:20:56.455
and obviously I just
reacted as well.

00:20:56.521 --> 00:20:57.522
But, yeah, it's these
belly scales.

00:20:57.589 --> 00:20:58.790
SIMON: Can you get him
off my thing?

00:20:58.857 --> 00:20:59.625
'Cause there's a lot
of pressure going on there.

00:20:59.691 --> 00:21:00.726
SIOUXSIE: Okay.

00:21:00.792 --> 00:21:01.994
SIMON: I don't like that.

00:21:02.060 --> 00:21:03.261
SIOUXSIE: At one point, when
the cobra was biting

00:21:03.328 --> 00:21:06.832
on Simon's glove, he did ask me
to release the grip.

00:21:06.898 --> 00:21:09.835
Like, oh, my God,
maybe it has gone through.

00:21:09.901 --> 00:21:12.170
SIMON: You can feel that
scratching, biting,

00:21:12.237 --> 00:21:13.639
chewing noise,

00:21:13.705 --> 00:21:15.574
and you can see the venom
sort of pouring out there

00:21:15.641 --> 00:21:16.808
from the fangs.

00:21:16.875 --> 00:21:17.909
He would have put a lot
of venom into me,

00:21:17.976 --> 00:21:19.911
because he wasn't happy at all.

00:21:19.978 --> 00:21:21.346
That's it. Okay.

00:21:21.413 --> 00:21:22.581
Maybe if I just slide
back up a bit.

00:21:22.648 --> 00:21:23.415
Is he alright? Yep.

00:21:23.482 --> 00:21:24.549
SIOUXSIE: Yeah, yeah.

00:21:24.616 --> 00:21:26.184
So go, move up, try and get
behind the head.

00:21:26.251 --> 00:21:27.619
SIMON: And do it again?
SIOUXSIE: Mm-hmm.

00:21:27.686 --> 00:21:29.321
SIMON: Yeah, I just felt like
my finger was getting hurt.

00:21:29.388 --> 00:21:31.223
SIOUXSIE: Ooh, it's getting
close. Are you alright?

00:21:31.289 --> 00:21:33.025
SIOUXSIE: Can you move up?
SIMON: What do I do?

00:21:33.091 --> 00:21:34.693
SIOUXSIE: Swap hands, try--
let me grab the body.

00:21:34.760 --> 00:21:35.694
SIMON: Hey, hey, hey, hey.

00:21:35.761 --> 00:21:37.262
SIOUXSIE: Yeah,
if I grab the body.

00:21:37.329 --> 00:21:39.064
SIMON: Right there.
SIOUXSIE: I've got the body.

00:21:39.131 --> 00:21:40.332
SIMON: I don't think
it's gone through,

00:21:40.399 --> 00:21:42.167
but it's not a pleasant feeling,
I'll be honest with you.

00:21:42.234 --> 00:21:44.369
SIOUXSIE: Should we check?
SIMON: Yeah, in a minute.

00:21:44.436 --> 00:21:47.406
SIMON: Very muscular snake, too,
and very, very fast.

00:21:47.472 --> 00:21:49.508
SIOUXSIE: But beautiful
condition, really stunning.

00:21:49.574 --> 00:21:50.676
SIMON: Yes, very good condition.

00:21:50.742 --> 00:21:52.778
SIOUXSIE: Brilliant.
SIMON: Perfect. Okay.

00:21:52.844 --> 00:21:54.446
SIOUXSIE: Bag it.
SIMON: Bag it.

00:21:54.513 --> 00:21:56.481
SIMON: That's alright,
not gonna do anything.

00:21:56.548 --> 00:21:57.716
One, two, three.

00:21:57.783 --> 00:21:59.217
SIOUXSIE: Okay.

00:21:59.284 --> 00:22:00.786
SIMON: That's it.

00:22:02.688 --> 00:22:04.389
That'll do.

00:22:07.192 --> 00:22:08.460
SIOUXSIE: Right.

00:22:08.527 --> 00:22:10.195
Contained.

00:22:10.262 --> 00:22:11.296
SIMON: Thank you, guys.

00:22:11.363 --> 00:22:13.732
Hopefully we won't see you
again today.

00:22:13.799 --> 00:22:15.367
Right, Sioux,
let's go find somewhere

00:22:15.434 --> 00:22:17.302
to release these snakes.

00:22:17.369 --> 00:22:18.503
SIOUXSIE: See you later.
MAN: Thank you very much.

00:22:18.570 --> 00:22:21.940
SIMON: Stay safe.
SIOUXSIE: Thank you, bye.

00:22:22.007 --> 00:22:23.475
SIMON: It's a hot day today,

00:22:23.542 --> 00:22:25.744
which means the snakes
in this city will be warmed up

00:22:25.811 --> 00:22:27.779
and on the hunt.

00:22:27.846 --> 00:22:31.283
It's going to get crazy busy
and even more intense,

00:22:31.349 --> 00:22:33.819
so we'd better release
these forest cobras quickly

00:22:33.885 --> 00:22:36.088
before the next calls come in.

00:22:37.923 --> 00:22:40.592
[phone rings]

00:22:40.659 --> 00:22:42.627
♪ ♪

00:22:42.694 --> 00:22:44.463
WOMAN: Thank you very much.
SIMON: Thank you.

00:22:45.931 --> 00:22:47.099
[woman screams]

00:22:47.165 --> 00:22:51.103
♪ ♪

00:22:51.169 --> 00:22:51.937
Hey, right there.

00:22:52.003 --> 00:22:53.205
[phone rings]

00:22:53.271 --> 00:22:54.372
Hello?

00:22:54.439 --> 00:22:55.974
A green snake?

00:22:56.041 --> 00:22:57.409
Okay, we're on our way.

00:22:57.476 --> 00:22:58.677
Just received a call.

00:22:58.744 --> 00:23:00.378
A very mixed up conversation.

00:23:00.445 --> 00:23:02.781
A green snake outside,
that's all we know.

00:23:02.848 --> 00:23:04.616
You know, when you're catching
green snakes,

00:23:04.683 --> 00:23:05.884
you've got to be very careful,

00:23:05.951 --> 00:23:07.552
because there are about
five or six different types

00:23:07.619 --> 00:23:10.355
of green snakes, so you don't
want to get it wrong.

00:23:10.422 --> 00:23:12.691
You know, it could be
a bush snake.

00:23:12.758 --> 00:23:13.792
That's harmless.

00:23:13.859 --> 00:23:15.494
It could be a natal green.
That's harmless.

00:23:15.560 --> 00:23:17.763
Western green snake, harmless.

00:23:17.829 --> 00:23:19.798
Green water snake, harmless.

00:23:19.865 --> 00:23:21.399
Boomslang, dangerous.

00:23:21.466 --> 00:23:23.268
Green mamba, deadly.

00:23:23.335 --> 00:23:25.804
You know, it's like,
what do I do?

00:23:37.516 --> 00:23:38.717
SIOUXSIE: Hiya,
you alright then?

00:23:38.784 --> 00:23:40.285
SIMON: Hi, you alright?
SIOUXSIE: You're locking up.

00:23:40.352 --> 00:23:41.386
SIMON: Yeah. Snake still there?

00:23:41.453 --> 00:23:42.654
MAN: You can see.

00:23:42.721 --> 00:23:43.922
SIOUXSIE: Is it still there?
Do you know what it is?

00:23:43.989 --> 00:23:45.056
Can you identify it?

00:23:45.123 --> 00:23:47.025
MAN: Green.
SIOUXSIE: It's green. Okay.

00:23:47.092 --> 00:23:47.993
SIMON: You've got to look
at the head of the snake

00:23:48.059 --> 00:23:49.394
to be able to tell
the difference,

00:23:49.461 --> 00:23:52.464
and get a, you know, try and
decide as fast as possible.

00:23:52.531 --> 00:23:54.766
Green mamba has got
a long, elongated face.

00:23:54.833 --> 00:23:57.502
It almost looks like
it's doing this...

00:23:57.569 --> 00:23:59.237
sucking its cheeks in.

00:23:59.304 --> 00:24:01.139
It's got a line, you'll see it,
a big smiley face,

00:24:01.206 --> 00:24:02.974
like an anvil-shaped head.

00:24:03.041 --> 00:24:04.743
If I grab it, or tell
Siouxsie to grab it,

00:24:04.810 --> 00:24:06.044
and it turns out to be
the wrong snake,

00:24:06.111 --> 00:24:07.612
that could be disastrous.

00:24:14.319 --> 00:24:16.354
SIMON: I can't see
anything yet.

00:24:16.421 --> 00:24:18.056
SIOUXSIE: I can't see it.

00:24:18.123 --> 00:24:19.324
SIMON: Oh, there it is.

00:24:19.391 --> 00:24:20.692
Down there, down there,
see that little green snake?

00:24:20.759 --> 00:24:23.428
SIOUXSIE: Oh, yeah, yeah,
I got it.

00:24:23.495 --> 00:24:25.430
SIMON: The green water snake
has no venom glands

00:24:25.497 --> 00:24:27.265
and is harmless to humans.

00:24:27.332 --> 00:24:30.101
But it looks almost identical
to a baby green mamba,

00:24:30.168 --> 00:24:32.404
which happens to be deadly.

00:24:32.470 --> 00:24:34.940
Green mamba's neurotoxic venom
is chemically similar

00:24:35.006 --> 00:24:37.142
to the venom of its
more famous cousin,

00:24:37.209 --> 00:24:41.046
the black mamba,
but much less toxic.

00:24:41.112 --> 00:24:44.583
Despite that, even a bite
from a 15-inch-long hatchling

00:24:44.649 --> 00:24:46.852
can cause a heart attack
and respiratory arrest

00:24:46.918 --> 00:24:48.820
in an adult human.

00:24:48.887 --> 00:24:50.021
SIOUXSIE: What is it?
SIMON: I don't know, wait there.

00:24:50.088 --> 00:24:51.857
SIMON: So we locate
the green snake,

00:24:51.923 --> 00:24:53.024
and I've got to make
a decision now,

00:24:53.091 --> 00:24:55.727
is it a safe snake or
is it a dangerous snake?

00:24:55.794 --> 00:24:56.595
SIOUXSIE: The herpetologist's
way to do it

00:24:56.661 --> 00:24:57.963
is to do a head scale count,

00:24:58.029 --> 00:25:00.298
check how many scales
on the head, between the eyes.

00:25:00.365 --> 00:25:01.700
We have no time for that.

00:25:01.766 --> 00:25:03.869
We haven't got time to sit there
and count and judge what it is,

00:25:03.935 --> 00:25:05.237
you know, we have to
grab it quick,

00:25:05.303 --> 00:25:07.906
and especially this snake,
it was really, really fast.

00:25:07.973 --> 00:25:10.208
SIMON: It's so fast,
it actually made a gap that way.

00:25:10.275 --> 00:25:11.209
SIOUXSIE: In this situation,

00:25:11.276 --> 00:25:12.444
for me, it's really,
really hard.

00:25:12.510 --> 00:25:16.214
I have to rely completely
on Simon's judgment.

00:25:16.281 --> 00:25:18.149
SIMON: Pull this table out,

00:25:18.216 --> 00:25:21.119
move it right the way
out the way, over to here.

00:25:24.789 --> 00:25:26.491
SIOUXSIE: Where is it?
I can't see it.

00:25:26.558 --> 00:25:29.194
SIMON: Behind there.
That is weird.

00:25:29.261 --> 00:25:30.362
SIOUXSIE: How strange.

00:25:30.428 --> 00:25:31.796
SIMON: It's just disappeared
into nowhere.

00:25:31.863 --> 00:25:34.232
You'll see it one second,
and then it's gone again,

00:25:34.299 --> 00:25:35.300
and I didn't even see the head,

00:25:35.367 --> 00:25:37.302
I could just see
the body go, 'bwwmmm!'

00:25:37.369 --> 00:25:38.603
Oh, no, where's it gone?
Where's it gone?

00:25:38.670 --> 00:25:41.106
I thinking, oh, is it a mamba?
You know, they are fast.

00:25:41.172 --> 00:25:42.374
SIOUXSIE: Green mambas
are really fast.

00:25:42.440 --> 00:25:45.510
So based on those factors,
looking at the snake,

00:25:45.577 --> 00:25:47.612
my thought is it, well,
you know, it could be a mamba.

00:25:47.679 --> 00:25:48.680
SIMON: I'm going to dig
around a bit.

00:25:48.747 --> 00:25:51.283
If it comes out,
and I say grab, grab.

00:25:51.349 --> 00:25:52.617
If I don't say grab,
don't grab it.

00:25:52.684 --> 00:25:54.119
SIOUXSIE: You don't know
what it is, do you?

00:25:54.185 --> 00:25:55.520
SIMON: No, it's a natal green.

00:25:55.587 --> 00:25:57.055
Just got to be 100% sure.

00:25:57.122 --> 00:25:58.023
SIOUXSIE: What do you say,
is it 100%?

00:25:58.089 --> 00:25:59.391
SIMON: I'm 90%.

00:25:59.457 --> 00:26:01.860
SIOUXSIE: Okay, I don't like
that 10% difference.

00:26:01.927 --> 00:26:02.861
SIMON: Ooh, okay.

00:26:02.928 --> 00:26:04.296
SIOUXSIE: His head poked
out the net.

00:26:04.362 --> 00:26:05.230
Ooh, he's going up, going up,
going up, going up, yeah.

00:26:05.297 --> 00:26:06.398
SIMON: Wait, wait, wait.

00:26:06.464 --> 00:26:07.699
I just want to double check
it isn't one.

00:26:07.766 --> 00:26:08.667
No, you're fine.

00:26:08.733 --> 00:26:10.435
Wait, wait, wait,
wait, wait, yep.

00:26:10.502 --> 00:26:11.569
Here we go.

00:26:11.636 --> 00:26:12.704
It is right,
it is a natal green,

00:26:12.771 --> 00:26:14.973
but just got to check
for a smiley face.

00:26:15.040 --> 00:26:16.241
You've only got a second
to make a decision

00:26:16.308 --> 00:26:17.075
whether to grab it or not.

00:26:17.142 --> 00:26:18.543
SIOUXSIE: You're happy?

00:26:18.610 --> 00:26:20.946
SIMON: Yeah, yeah. We can have
a closer look at it in a second.

00:26:21.012 --> 00:26:22.981
SIMON: Oh. Ugh.
SIOUXSIE: Must.

00:26:23.048 --> 00:26:23.915
SIMON: Smell that.
SIOUXSIE: Lovely.

00:26:23.982 --> 00:26:25.317
SIMON: That's really pleasant.

00:26:25.383 --> 00:26:29.254
After a while I managed to get
a look at the head of it,

00:26:29.321 --> 00:26:32.090
and I'm saying to Sioux,
no, it's a green water snake

00:26:32.157 --> 00:26:34.125
or a natal green snake,
grab it if it goes your way,

00:26:34.192 --> 00:26:35.327
and then I can see her going,

00:26:35.393 --> 00:26:36.962
are you sure it's not a mamba,
are you sure?

00:26:37.028 --> 00:26:38.229
And I thought to myself,

00:26:38.296 --> 00:26:39.698
I better make sure again,
hadn't I?

00:26:39.764 --> 00:26:40.966
So I'm looking
for the head again,

00:26:41.032 --> 00:26:42.334
and I'm fishing around,
and then I saw it.

00:26:42.400 --> 00:26:45.503
Yeah, good to go, and then
it shot my way and I grabbed it.

00:26:45.570 --> 00:26:49.407
Yeah, it's a natal green,
a water snake.

00:26:49.474 --> 00:26:51.609
Beautiful green snake, I'll get
it back out the bag now.

00:26:51.676 --> 00:26:52.444
You know, you just got
to make sure

00:26:52.510 --> 00:26:54.512
before you grab any green snake,

00:26:54.579 --> 00:26:57.048
they do really resemble
a green mamba.

00:26:57.115 --> 00:27:01.519
The only thing that's lacking
is a big, smiley mouth.

00:27:01.586 --> 00:27:03.822
So you can see there, it doesn't
have the lips, you know,

00:27:03.888 --> 00:27:06.524
like the green mamba,
potentially like that.

00:27:06.591 --> 00:27:08.693
This little snake
doesn't have that.

00:27:08.760 --> 00:27:09.928
SIOUXSIE: Pretty.

00:27:09.995 --> 00:27:12.397
SIMON: Yeah, very pretty snake,
very fast moving,

00:27:12.464 --> 00:27:14.766
and can disappear, as you saw
there, in half a second.

00:27:14.833 --> 00:27:15.834
We didn't even know
where it went.

00:27:15.900 --> 00:27:17.535
Familiarize yourself with that.

00:27:17.602 --> 00:27:19.437
Sometimes they've got more
of a blue speckling on him.

00:27:19.504 --> 00:27:20.972
SIOUXSIE: I'd say there is,
isn't there, here.

00:27:21.039 --> 00:27:22.273
SIMON: Yeah.

00:27:22.340 --> 00:27:24.642
That's a nice snake to catch,
we don't catch many.

00:27:24.709 --> 00:27:26.811
He'll get about twice that size.

00:27:26.878 --> 00:27:31.216
About as thick as your second
finger, something like that.

00:27:31.282 --> 00:27:32.684
SIOUXSIE: Come on,
I'm holding it.

00:27:32.751 --> 00:27:34.853
You're fine. I've got the head
so nothing can happen to you.

00:27:34.919 --> 00:27:37.722
So have a touch,
he feels beautiful.

00:27:37.789 --> 00:27:40.158
Are you okay?

00:27:40.225 --> 00:27:42.127
You alright there?
Are you going to have a go?

00:27:42.193 --> 00:27:43.061
[laughs]

00:27:48.066 --> 00:27:48.900
SIMON: That's alright.
You did the right thing.

00:27:48.967 --> 00:27:50.168
You just keep an eye on it.

00:27:50.235 --> 00:27:51.436
SIOUXSIE: Okay, see,
you've got it, it's on you.

00:27:51.503 --> 00:27:53.505
You're brave.
I've got the head, don't worry.

00:27:53.571 --> 00:27:57.342
SIMON: To the untrained eye,
the harmless green varieties

00:27:57.409 --> 00:27:58.710
generally get killed on site

00:27:58.777 --> 00:28:02.213
because people think it's
a green mamba, which is sad.

00:28:02.280 --> 00:28:04.115
So it was quite nice
to capture this one

00:28:04.182 --> 00:28:05.483
and get it off to safety.

00:28:05.550 --> 00:28:13.391
♪ ♪

00:28:13.458 --> 00:28:16.327
We release every single
snake we catch.

00:28:16.394 --> 00:28:18.530
I get a great feeling afterwards
when I've let a snake go,

00:28:18.596 --> 00:28:19.864
and I see it disappear
into the bush,

00:28:19.931 --> 00:28:21.900
and I hope I don't see it again.

00:28:21.966 --> 00:28:26.571
♪ ♪

00:28:30.508 --> 00:28:32.010
SIOUXSIE: So is there some,
a pond you've got,

00:28:32.077 --> 00:28:33.545
you know about, in here?

00:28:33.611 --> 00:28:36.181
SIMON: Yeah, yeah,
it's the perfect place for it.

00:28:39.617 --> 00:28:41.619
Yeah, see, it's right here.

00:28:41.686 --> 00:28:43.054
SIOUXSIE: Oh, it's perfect.

00:28:43.121 --> 00:28:44.222
SIMON: Yep, there's frogs
in here, there's fish in here,

00:28:44.289 --> 00:28:45.590
there's all sorts in here.

00:28:45.657 --> 00:28:47.158
SIOUXSIE: He'll be really happy,
won't he?

00:28:47.225 --> 00:28:48.426
SIMON: Yeah, yeah,
he'll be fine.

00:28:48.493 --> 00:28:49.694
I've let loads of snakes
go here.

00:28:49.761 --> 00:28:52.931
SIOUXSIE: Have you?
SIMON: Yeah, over the years.

00:28:52.997 --> 00:28:54.199
SIOUXSIE: So, this is man-made,
is it?

00:28:54.265 --> 00:28:57.102
SIMON: It's a man-made pond
in a nature reserve.

00:28:57.168 --> 00:28:58.403
Over here will do.

00:28:58.470 --> 00:28:59.337
SIOUXSIE: Just over there, yeah?

00:28:59.404 --> 00:29:01.339
SIMON: Perfect.

00:29:03.308 --> 00:29:05.477
[phone ringing]

00:29:05.543 --> 00:29:06.678
I haven't got nails.

00:29:06.744 --> 00:29:07.812
Hello?

00:29:07.879 --> 00:29:09.080
Black mamba.

00:29:09.147 --> 00:29:10.348
We'll be there
as fast as we can.

00:29:10.415 --> 00:29:11.716
We have to let this thing
go now, and then go.

00:29:11.783 --> 00:29:13.051
Okay, we're on our way,
okay, okay?

00:29:13.118 --> 00:29:14.052
Yeah, cheers.
Text me the address.

00:29:14.119 --> 00:29:15.086
Right, bye, bye, bye.

00:29:15.153 --> 00:29:16.454
We have to go do this,
let it go.

00:29:16.521 --> 00:29:18.356
Put it down there and let's go.

00:29:18.423 --> 00:29:21.593
You alright, get the lid off?

00:29:21.659 --> 00:29:23.995
SIOUXSIE: Ready?
SIMON: Bye-bye, snake.

00:29:24.062 --> 00:29:24.863
SIOUXSIE: Just leave it
and do it?

00:29:24.929 --> 00:29:27.232
SIMON: Yeah, yeah, let him go.

00:29:32.303 --> 00:29:33.171
SIOUXSIE:
Perfect, look at him.

00:29:33.238 --> 00:29:34.305
SIMON: There we go.

00:29:34.372 --> 00:29:35.640
SIOUXSIE:
Yeah, oh, look how fast he is.

00:29:35.707 --> 00:29:38.710
SIMON: Yeah, there you go.
Perfect swimmer, bye-bye.

00:29:38.776 --> 00:29:40.044
SIOUXSIE: Yeah, he's quick.

00:29:40.111 --> 00:29:41.613
That's really good.

00:29:41.679 --> 00:29:42.914
Right, mamba.

00:29:42.981 --> 00:29:44.516
SIMON: Right, let's go. Mamba.

00:29:44.582 --> 00:29:57.795
♪ ♪

00:29:57.862 --> 00:29:58.796
SIMON: It doesn't matter
how many times

00:29:58.863 --> 00:30:00.064
you catch a black mamba,

00:30:00.131 --> 00:30:04.102
it is always that thing of fear,
excitement, adrenaline,

00:30:04.169 --> 00:30:07.605
and worrying, you know,
if you cock up,

00:30:07.672 --> 00:30:09.240
could this be the last one
you catch?

00:30:09.307 --> 00:30:10.708
That goes through your mind
all the time.

00:30:10.775 --> 00:30:13.244
The best snake catchers
in the world get bitten.

00:30:13.311 --> 00:30:15.013
It's just one of those jobs,
you know.

00:30:15.079 --> 00:30:17.015
I think if it didn't,
if you didn't think like that,

00:30:17.081 --> 00:30:18.983
you wouldn't be normal.

00:30:19.050 --> 00:30:29.460
♪ ♪

00:30:29.527 --> 00:30:31.963
[phone ringing]

00:30:32.030 --> 00:30:33.865
The owner of the house
is freaking out,

00:30:33.932 --> 00:30:34.933
asking where we are.

00:30:34.999 --> 00:30:36.901
[phone ringing]

00:30:36.968 --> 00:30:38.336
Yeah, just, just keep
an eye on the snake,

00:30:38.403 --> 00:30:39.437
don't interfere with it,

00:30:39.504 --> 00:30:41.539
and we'll be there
as quick as we can.

00:30:41.606 --> 00:30:52.450
♪ ♪

00:30:56.454 --> 00:30:57.322
Where am I parking?

00:30:57.388 --> 00:30:59.591
Oh, there? Yeah.

00:31:03.361 --> 00:31:04.796
SIOUXSIE: Do you have
the grabbers?

00:31:04.862 --> 00:31:06.064
SIMON: No, that's it.

00:31:06.130 --> 00:31:07.799
Okay.

00:31:07.865 --> 00:31:08.900
This house here?

00:31:08.967 --> 00:31:09.968
Okay.

00:31:10.034 --> 00:31:10.802
SIOUXSIE:
Did you lock the door?

00:31:10.868 --> 00:31:12.470
SIMON: Yeah.

00:31:16.074 --> 00:31:16.975
How's it, guys?

00:31:17.041 --> 00:31:18.943
MAN: Good.
SIMON: Right.

00:31:20.111 --> 00:31:21.479
SIMON: Oh, thanks.

00:31:21.546 --> 00:31:22.780
Right, show me where.

00:31:22.847 --> 00:31:24.682
MAN: Between this,
it's facing that way.

00:31:24.749 --> 00:31:25.683
SIOUXSIE: Hiya,
are you alright?

00:31:25.750 --> 00:31:27.051
MAN: It's standing
with the tail.

00:31:27.118 --> 00:31:29.087
SIMON: Gray, black snake,
yeah? Big?

00:31:30.755 --> 00:31:32.624
SIMON: Like a whiter color?
Yeah, yeah, yeah, okay.

00:31:32.690 --> 00:31:33.658
SIOUXSIE: A mamba, yeah?

00:31:33.725 --> 00:31:35.593
SIMON: So, yeah.
Okay, we're here now.

00:31:35.660 --> 00:31:37.228
A black mamba's got inside.

00:31:37.295 --> 00:31:38.930
Obviously there's a lot of stuff
going on in there.

00:31:38.997 --> 00:31:41.032
There's potatoes everywhere,
there's fridges pulled out,

00:31:41.099 --> 00:31:42.467
and it's gone behind
one of the cupboards here.

00:31:42.533 --> 00:31:46.704
So, I'm just going to go in now
and take it from there, right?

00:31:49.240 --> 00:31:51.342
SIOUXSIE: So they think--oh,
my God, I can't see anywhere.

00:31:51.409 --> 00:31:52.910
They think it's behind the door?

00:31:52.977 --> 00:31:55.647
SIMON: Yeah, somewhere up there.

00:31:55.713 --> 00:31:57.649
Doesn't matter how many times
you catch a mamba,

00:31:57.715 --> 00:31:59.217
your adrenaline is
always pumping.

00:31:59.284 --> 00:32:01.052
There's so much going through
your head at the time,

00:32:01.119 --> 00:32:02.320
and the situation,

00:32:02.387 --> 00:32:03.921
and so many things that could
possibly go wrong.

00:32:03.988 --> 00:32:06.524
And you are dealing with one of
the fastest snakes in the world,

00:32:06.591 --> 00:32:08.760
probably the most feared snake
in the world.

00:32:08.826 --> 00:32:13.631
The black mamba is not a toy,
it is one serious snake.

00:32:13.698 --> 00:32:15.633
The black mamba's potent venom,

00:32:15.700 --> 00:32:17.769
plus the massive amount
it injects,

00:32:17.835 --> 00:32:20.271
makes for a deadly bite.

00:32:20.338 --> 00:32:23.708
Its venom is both neurotoxic
and cardiotoxic,

00:32:23.775 --> 00:32:26.210
meaning it affects
the entire nervous system

00:32:26.277 --> 00:32:28.212
as well as the heart.

00:32:28.279 --> 00:32:31.649
Initially there will be pain and
numbness around the bite site,

00:32:31.716 --> 00:32:34.686
swiftly followed
by headaches, drooling,

00:32:34.752 --> 00:32:38.790
nosebleeds, vomiting,
and diarrhea.

00:32:38.856 --> 00:32:40.224
Paralysis follows,

00:32:40.291 --> 00:32:43.561
including a lack of ability
to blink or swallow.

00:32:43.628 --> 00:32:45.530
The lungs stop functioning.

00:32:45.596 --> 00:32:47.365
Then the heart stops.

00:32:47.432 --> 00:32:49.233
So you last saw it on the floor
or the top?

00:32:50.601 --> 00:32:53.938
SIMON: Okay, alright,
let's just make a bit of...

00:32:54.005 --> 00:32:56.774
Yeah, alright, let's just
make a bit of space.

00:32:56.841 --> 00:32:59.110
This thing, wants to move it,
move it.

00:32:59.177 --> 00:32:59.944
SIOUXSIE: Let me get
the torch ready.

00:33:00.011 --> 00:33:02.280
SIMON: Get one torch out.

00:33:12.757 --> 00:33:15.693
Okay.

00:33:15.760 --> 00:33:18.429
Okay. Can't see anything.

00:33:27.372 --> 00:33:29.507
It's not under there.

00:33:29.574 --> 00:33:30.375
MAN: Now he's up there again.

00:33:30.441 --> 00:33:31.209
SIMON: Went up there?

00:33:32.410 --> 00:33:34.245
SIMON: Okay, in, inside?

00:33:34.312 --> 00:33:36.047
Inside the wardrobe?

00:33:36.114 --> 00:33:37.482
Okay, alright, alright.

00:33:37.548 --> 00:33:40.218
When you're dealing with a
black mamba in a confined space,

00:33:40.284 --> 00:33:41.486
like a wardrobe,

00:33:41.552 --> 00:33:42.754
you know, you can't just go
sticking your hands in.

00:33:42.820 --> 00:33:43.888
You don't know where it is,

00:33:43.955 --> 00:33:45.356
maybe there's a lot of stuff
in the wardrobe.

00:33:45.423 --> 00:33:48.326
It's not a case of just
taking everything out

00:33:48.393 --> 00:33:49.627
and waiting for it to come out.

00:33:49.694 --> 00:33:50.862
You know, you just don't know
what's going to happen,

00:33:50.928 --> 00:33:51.996
you know?

00:33:52.063 --> 00:33:53.364
It's one of the fastest
snakes in the world.

00:33:53.431 --> 00:33:56.067
Siouxsie, if I grab it, you must
just bang another grabber

00:33:56.134 --> 00:33:57.802
on midsection, anywhere.

00:33:57.869 --> 00:33:59.804
Anywhere you can, but not,
obviously, too close

00:33:59.871 --> 00:34:02.306
to where I'm going to put mine.

00:34:04.475 --> 00:34:06.711
SIOUXSIE: If we're relying on
this person's description,

00:34:06.778 --> 00:34:07.879
you know, it's a lot to rely on,

00:34:07.945 --> 00:34:09.180
because if we're walking around

00:34:09.247 --> 00:34:10.882
and the snake isn't
in the wardrobe,

00:34:10.948 --> 00:34:12.250
potentially we're going
to tread on it,

00:34:12.316 --> 00:34:14.285
or it's going to fly out,
you know, at us.

00:34:14.352 --> 00:34:16.020
So it's really,
really dangerous.

00:34:20.324 --> 00:34:21.759
SIMON: Behind it?

00:34:21.826 --> 00:34:24.729
SIMON: There?
MAN: Yeah, yeah.

00:34:24.796 --> 00:34:26.497
SIMON: There's nothing there.

00:34:30.601 --> 00:34:31.669
SIMON: It might still be
in the cupboard, though.

00:34:31.736 --> 00:34:32.670
MAN: Inside the bathroom.

00:34:32.737 --> 00:34:33.805
SIMON: Inside the bathroom,
in here?

00:34:33.871 --> 00:34:35.506
MAN: Yeah.

00:34:40.578 --> 00:34:43.314
SIMON: Not in here. Not there.

00:34:43.381 --> 00:34:44.582
Maybe it's still
inside the wardrobe?

00:34:44.649 --> 00:34:46.350
MAN: Yeah.
SIMON: Yeah.

00:34:46.417 --> 00:34:47.819
SIOUXSIE: I'll keep an eye
on this side.

00:34:47.885 --> 00:34:49.420
SIMON: Yeah, just watch there.

00:34:49.487 --> 00:34:51.722
No, here, here, here, here!

00:34:51.789 --> 00:34:53.024
Right, it's huge.

00:34:53.090 --> 00:34:54.125
SIOUXSIE: A mamba? Black mamba?

00:34:54.192 --> 00:34:55.726
SIMON: Big black mamba.

00:34:55.793 --> 00:34:58.229
Mama. Great, get another
grabber, quick.

00:34:58.296 --> 00:35:00.298
And I just see
this big banana shape

00:35:00.364 --> 00:35:02.033
of black, thick, thick, thick,

00:35:02.099 --> 00:35:04.569
whoa, that's a big black mamba.

00:35:04.635 --> 00:35:05.837
Two. Bang one on there.

00:35:05.903 --> 00:35:06.671
SIOUXSIE: Where? There?

00:35:06.737 --> 00:35:08.506
SIMON: Anywhere.

00:35:10.541 --> 00:35:12.977
There, wait, it's gone through
the coat hanger, maybe,

00:35:13.044 --> 00:35:16.481
let go of it, let him come out.
let go, let go.

00:35:16.547 --> 00:35:18.049
SIOUXSIE: Oh, it's a good size.

00:35:18.115 --> 00:35:20.418
SIMON: Stand up on that bed.

00:35:23.688 --> 00:35:25.022
It's going down.

00:35:25.089 --> 00:35:27.358
I'm going to move the snake
onto that there, okay, if I can.

00:35:27.425 --> 00:35:29.360
Watch yourself.

00:35:29.427 --> 00:35:32.129
Right, it's still
in the cupboard.

00:35:32.196 --> 00:35:35.533
Where's it going, where's it
going, where's it going?

00:35:35.600 --> 00:35:37.068
Where's it going?

00:35:37.134 --> 00:35:38.336
SIOUXSIE: Right.
It's contained this side.

00:35:38.402 --> 00:35:39.537
SIMON: Just keep an eye
out that side, guys,

00:35:39.604 --> 00:35:42.406
'cause I can't see
behind this wardrobe.

00:35:42.473 --> 00:35:44.342
Where's it gone?

00:35:48.746 --> 00:35:50.314
Where's it gone?
Where's it gone?

00:35:50.381 --> 00:35:52.717
Grab me a torch.

00:35:57.688 --> 00:35:58.456
[gasps]
Watch out.

00:35:58.523 --> 00:36:00.224
Whoa, okay, it's striking now.

00:36:00.291 --> 00:36:02.827
Don't need the torch,
put it on the bed.

00:36:02.894 --> 00:36:04.228
He means business, this one.

00:36:04.295 --> 00:36:06.030
Okay.

00:36:06.097 --> 00:36:07.532
Very slowly, slowly.

00:36:07.598 --> 00:36:08.900
Yeah, you open your mouth.

00:36:08.966 --> 00:36:11.035
Wha! Like this big flash
of black mouth,

00:36:11.102 --> 00:36:12.236
sticks his head
out the wardrobe,

00:36:12.303 --> 00:36:13.804
it's like, hey,
hang on a minute.

00:36:13.871 --> 00:36:14.906
SIOUXSIE: You see the mouth,

00:36:14.972 --> 00:36:16.941
the animal that delivers
the kiss of death,

00:36:17.008 --> 00:36:18.376
and it's staring at me.

00:36:18.442 --> 00:36:19.944
And do you of sort of think,
what the hell am I doing here,

00:36:20.011 --> 00:36:21.379
why am I doing this?

00:36:21.445 --> 00:36:23.381
SIMON: I need a torch.

00:36:23.447 --> 00:36:25.583
It's going mental.
Quickly, get that thing on.

00:36:25.650 --> 00:36:28.920
No, no, oh, not flashing.

00:36:30.988 --> 00:36:32.757
SIOUXSIE: Blimey.

00:36:33.991 --> 00:36:35.927
SIMON: In a confined space
like that,

00:36:35.993 --> 00:36:37.628
you've got to be quick
to get out the way,

00:36:37.695 --> 00:36:39.597
and even faster to try
and get a tong on it,

00:36:39.664 --> 00:36:41.198
to get a grab stick on it fast.

00:36:41.265 --> 00:36:43.200
And it's not easy to do that,
you know.

00:36:43.267 --> 00:36:45.303
Firstly, for Sioux,
it's quite hard for her,

00:36:45.369 --> 00:36:46.737
because she's got tiny hands,

00:36:46.804 --> 00:36:49.140
like, her hands fit in the palm
of my hand.

00:36:49.206 --> 00:36:50.141
She's got kid's hands.

00:36:50.207 --> 00:36:51.542
Look at my hands, they're huge.

00:36:51.609 --> 00:36:54.845
I can use the tongs
with one hand.

00:36:54.912 --> 00:36:57.048
SIOUXSIE: Let's get gloves.

00:36:57.114 --> 00:37:00.051
SIMON: So I see Siouxsie lifting
up the tongs like this,

00:37:00.117 --> 00:37:01.252
and trying to go for it.

00:37:01.319 --> 00:37:03.187
And I'm saying just grab
the bloody thing!

00:37:03.254 --> 00:37:05.089
Put a grab stick on there,
just as quick as you can,

00:37:05.156 --> 00:37:07.191
just hold it anywhere,
it doesn't matter.

00:37:07.258 --> 00:37:08.859
Bang another grab,
bang another grab.

00:37:08.926 --> 00:37:10.494
Quick, bang another grab.

00:37:10.561 --> 00:37:12.163
Get it on there, get it
on there, get it on there.

00:37:12.229 --> 00:37:13.598
SIOUXSIE: It's on there.
It's not good, hold on.

00:37:13.664 --> 00:37:14.432
SIMON: Just get one on it.

00:37:14.498 --> 00:37:16.233
SIOUXSIE: I am, I am, I am.

00:37:16.300 --> 00:37:17.535
On.

00:37:17.602 --> 00:37:18.970
SIMON: Keep that tight.
Don't let go, whatever you do.

00:37:19.036 --> 00:37:20.705
SIOUXSIE: Tight.

00:37:22.907 --> 00:37:24.475
SIMON: Letting go.
Don't let go, don't let go.

00:37:24.542 --> 00:37:26.477
SIOUXSIE:
I'm not letting go.

00:37:26.544 --> 00:37:28.579
SIMON: Now, you can let go,
in a second.

00:37:28.646 --> 00:37:29.914
SIOUXSIE: Have you got
a good grip?

00:37:29.981 --> 00:37:31.182
SIMON: Yeah, I've got it,
I've got it, okay, let go.

00:37:31.248 --> 00:37:33.317
SIOUXSIE: You've got it? Happy?

00:37:33.384 --> 00:37:35.219
Oh, that's big.

00:37:35.286 --> 00:37:37.788
[whistles]

00:37:37.855 --> 00:37:38.856
SIMON: Big black mamba.

00:37:38.923 --> 00:37:40.958
[laughs]
This is a good...

00:37:41.025 --> 00:37:45.463
I'd have to measure it,
but hold the tail there.

00:37:45.529 --> 00:37:47.832
It's a big, old...
[whistles]

00:37:47.898 --> 00:37:49.634
It's just scenting all over you,
watch out.

00:37:49.700 --> 00:37:51.035
Just let him do that. Right.

00:37:51.102 --> 00:37:55.373
That's probably getting close to
3 meters, I would say, 2.6, 2.7.

00:37:55.439 --> 00:37:57.475
Would have to measure it,
but anyway it's big.

00:37:57.541 --> 00:37:58.843
Let's move outside.

00:37:58.909 --> 00:37:59.810
SIOUXSIE: Tools there.

00:37:59.877 --> 00:38:02.446
SIMON: Need to bring
the tools.

00:38:02.513 --> 00:38:03.748
Come back and get them.

00:38:03.814 --> 00:38:06.350
Just reel it out, we'll come
back and get the tools.

00:38:08.552 --> 00:38:10.421
Tail it out, tail it out.

00:38:12.790 --> 00:38:13.824
Okay.

00:38:13.891 --> 00:38:16.093
If you run back and
get the grabbers.

00:38:18.629 --> 00:38:19.930
Run back and get the grabs.

00:38:19.997 --> 00:38:20.865
SIOUXSIE: I let all that go.

00:38:20.931 --> 00:38:22.633
SIMON: Nine, ten-foot snake.

00:38:22.700 --> 00:38:25.069
Pumped up, very warm,
angry, upset,

00:38:25.136 --> 00:38:27.271
and most importantly,
very, very scared.

00:38:27.338 --> 00:38:29.573
This is obviously the most
dangerous part for us,

00:38:29.640 --> 00:38:31.809
because if you slip,
then you got a big problem.

00:38:31.876 --> 00:38:34.945
You've got something in your
hand that is potentially lethal,

00:38:35.012 --> 00:38:36.247
and you need to get it
into that bag.

00:38:36.313 --> 00:38:38.416
So it's very, very important
you don't mess this up.

00:38:38.482 --> 00:38:39.950
It's not an easy thing to do.

00:38:40.017 --> 00:38:42.520
You can't just shove your arm
in a pillowcase

00:38:42.586 --> 00:38:45.923
and then just sort of, like,
go like that and it goes in.

00:38:45.990 --> 00:38:47.525
It doesn't,
it doesn't work like that.

00:38:47.591 --> 00:38:49.260
Alright, alright.

00:38:51.796 --> 00:38:54.598
All we need is a pillowcase.

00:38:54.665 --> 00:38:56.734
Okay, what I'm going to do...
Everyone just stay back, okay?

00:38:56.801 --> 00:38:58.202
And don't touch the snake
or anything like that,

00:38:58.269 --> 00:39:10.948
because this is very dangerous,
what I'm about to do.

00:39:11.015 --> 00:39:16.687
SIMON: Put my other arm into
the pillowcase, into the corner.

00:39:16.754 --> 00:39:17.521
Don't go anywhere near that.

00:39:17.588 --> 00:39:20.357
SIOUXSIE: No, no, no.

00:39:20.424 --> 00:39:21.959
SIMON: Just hold that there
for a second.

00:39:22.026 --> 00:39:23.327
SIOUXSIE: Do you want me
to hold it?

00:39:23.394 --> 00:39:24.428
SIMON: Just hold it, yeah,
just hold that for a second.

00:39:24.495 --> 00:39:26.197
I'll do it after, that's fine.

00:39:26.263 --> 00:39:29.500
Okay, so I've got the
black mamba in my right hand,

00:39:29.567 --> 00:39:31.635
and somehow I've got to get it
into the pillowcase,

00:39:31.702 --> 00:39:33.137
which will be in my left hand.

00:39:33.204 --> 00:39:35.840
It's very hard to explain, but
basically what you've got to do

00:39:35.906 --> 00:39:37.775
is you've got to feed
the pillowcase

00:39:37.842 --> 00:39:39.510
underneath the black mamba,

00:39:39.577 --> 00:39:42.413
touching your hand
with the snake,

00:39:42.480 --> 00:39:43.814
and gradually,
and very, very slowly,

00:39:43.881 --> 00:39:45.449
you have to exchange hands.

00:39:45.516 --> 00:39:47.585
So now the snake was
in my right hand,

00:39:47.651 --> 00:39:49.120
and now it needs to
be in my left hand,

00:39:49.186 --> 00:39:50.654
with the pillowcase around it.

00:39:50.721 --> 00:39:52.356
Very fiddly thing to do.

00:39:52.423 --> 00:39:54.091
If you haven't got
the snake correctly,

00:39:54.158 --> 00:39:55.960
it can turn and bite,
turn and bite you.

00:39:56.026 --> 00:39:59.130
Contort its head, its face,
and it will get you.

00:39:59.196 --> 00:40:01.465
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

00:40:04.902 --> 00:40:06.871
Tail.

00:40:10.274 --> 00:40:13.444
Just unravel it.

00:40:13.511 --> 00:40:16.447
Alright, snake, I'm going
to get you out of here.

00:40:24.955 --> 00:40:26.490
You know, what you're doing
is a dangerous job.

00:40:26.557 --> 00:40:28.559
It's like being a bomb disposal
expert, you know?

00:40:28.626 --> 00:40:30.461
It must go through their minds
as well, you know,

00:40:30.528 --> 00:40:33.197
if I cut the wrong wire, am I
just going to see a big flash

00:40:33.264 --> 00:40:34.365
and that's the end of me?

00:40:34.431 --> 00:40:35.633
It's the same type of thing.

00:40:35.699 --> 00:40:37.201
If you get bitten
by a black mamba,

00:40:37.268 --> 00:40:40.271
you could be, you might be lucky
and get to hospital,

00:40:40.337 --> 00:40:42.273
you might be dead in five,
ten minutes, you know.

00:40:42.339 --> 00:40:43.808
It is really one
of those situations.

00:40:43.874 --> 00:40:45.576
And you think, you've got
this snake behind the head,

00:40:45.643 --> 00:40:47.912
it's fearing for its life,

00:40:47.978 --> 00:40:51.148
it's going to inject you with
however much it can, you know,

00:40:51.215 --> 00:40:52.349
it's not going to be
a small dose,

00:40:52.416 --> 00:40:54.318
it's going to pump you
full of that [bleep],

00:40:54.385 --> 00:40:56.754
and then you're in big trouble.

00:40:56.821 --> 00:40:58.789
Chuck all that, pull that
all the way down.

00:40:58.856 --> 00:41:01.192
Chuck it all in, chuck it in.

00:41:01.258 --> 00:41:03.394
Chuck it all in, chuck it
all in, chuck it all in.

00:41:03.460 --> 00:41:04.562
SIOUXSIE: It's in.
SIMON: Put it all in.

00:41:04.628 --> 00:41:06.263
SIOUXSIE: It's in.
That looks good.

00:41:06.330 --> 00:41:08.299
SIMON: Right, you're going
to put that on the floor.

00:41:08.365 --> 00:41:09.567
SIOUXSIE: Do you want gloves
on this?

00:41:09.633 --> 00:41:13.671
SIMON: No, no. Just get the bar,
no, get the grabber.

00:41:13.737 --> 00:41:16.173
Just get a...
yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:41:16.240 --> 00:41:19.476
Push it there on the floor,
flatten it.

00:41:19.543 --> 00:41:21.378
Push it all the way.

00:41:21.445 --> 00:41:22.546
SIOUXSIE: It could still jump,
though.

00:41:22.613 --> 00:41:24.515
SIMON: Yeah.

00:41:24.582 --> 00:41:25.683
Come on, get down.

00:41:25.749 --> 00:41:27.051
See all that on the pillowcase
there, guys?

00:41:27.117 --> 00:41:28.185
That's venom.

00:41:28.252 --> 00:41:29.186
There's a bit of blood as well.

00:41:29.253 --> 00:41:30.588
There's an injury to the snake,
I think.

00:41:30.654 --> 00:41:32.189
Do you guys, did anyone
hit the snake or anything

00:41:32.256 --> 00:41:33.858
when it went inside?

00:41:33.924 --> 00:41:36.427
No one? Nothing? Okay.

00:41:36.493 --> 00:41:37.261
Good.

00:41:37.328 --> 00:41:39.930
You did the right thing not to.

00:41:39.997 --> 00:41:41.732
Can you now get the tape,

00:41:41.799 --> 00:41:43.968
just twist it round
as far as you can.

00:41:44.034 --> 00:41:45.202
Keep going, keep going.

00:41:45.269 --> 00:41:47.071
Pull, pull the sack as well,
at the same time.

00:41:47.137 --> 00:41:48.038
The tighter the better, tighter.

00:41:48.105 --> 00:41:49.039
SIOUXSIE: Is that,
just like that?

00:41:49.106 --> 00:41:50.374
SIMON: No, no, I've got
his head there.

00:41:50.441 --> 00:41:51.342
SIOUXSIE: No, I know.
I've got him by the tail.

00:41:51.408 --> 00:41:53.878
SIMON: No, no. Tape it.

00:41:53.944 --> 00:41:54.778
SIOUXSIE:
Yeah, can you hold it?

00:41:54.845 --> 00:41:57.414
SIMON: Tape that.

00:41:57.481 --> 00:41:58.449
SIOUXSIE: Lower?

00:41:58.515 --> 00:41:59.650
SIMON: Just go around
a few times.

00:41:59.717 --> 00:42:00.951
Remember, I've still
got his head.

00:42:01.018 --> 00:42:01.952
Can't let go of the head.

00:42:02.019 --> 00:42:03.053
If you let go of the head,

00:42:03.120 --> 00:42:04.321
it will bite you
straight through the bag,

00:42:04.388 --> 00:42:06.390
so that's the last thing you do,
is release the head.

00:42:06.457 --> 00:42:09.260
Okay, move out the way.

00:42:09.326 --> 00:42:11.562
One, two, three.

00:42:13.030 --> 00:42:15.065
SIOUXSIE: Woo!

00:42:15.132 --> 00:42:16.200
SIMON: Don't, no one touch
the bag, okay?

00:42:16.267 --> 00:42:17.601
It'll bite you through the bag.

00:42:17.668 --> 00:42:19.470
It'll still kill you,
no problem.

00:42:19.536 --> 00:42:22.039
And then what we'll do...

00:42:22.106 --> 00:42:25.142
Just leave that one. There.
Give me that other grab.

00:42:30.180 --> 00:42:32.449
There. Watch your fingers.

00:42:32.516 --> 00:42:33.584
Well done.

00:42:33.651 --> 00:42:34.785
Dangerous.

00:42:34.852 --> 00:42:36.387
That's it.

00:42:38.856 --> 00:42:39.924
SIOUXSIE: Right. Contained.

00:42:39.990 --> 00:42:42.893
SIMON: Okay, safe.

00:42:42.960 --> 00:42:45.229
Snake's contained,
everybody's safe,

00:42:45.296 --> 00:42:46.897
and then you can relax
for half a second.

00:42:46.964 --> 00:42:50.634
You know, you can calm down
to panic mode now.

00:42:50.701 --> 00:42:52.269
You know, after doing that,
you think to yourself,

00:42:52.336 --> 00:42:55.039
I must be bloody nuts.

00:42:58.976 --> 00:43:00.978
Yeah, that's from gripping...

00:43:01.045 --> 00:43:02.613
So you were inside
when the snake came in?

00:43:03.948 --> 00:43:05.349
SIMON: Yeah, I bet you
got a fright, eh?

00:43:06.917 --> 00:43:09.019
[laughter]

00:43:09.086 --> 00:43:10.721
SIMON: I'd also jump
through the window, don't worry.

00:43:10.788 --> 00:43:12.256
That's very dangerous.

00:43:12.323 --> 00:43:13.390
SIOUXSIE: Imagine putting
your hand in to get something

00:43:13.457 --> 00:43:14.792
out the wardrobe...

00:43:14.858 --> 00:43:17.328
SIMON: Yeah, imagine you went to
put your shirt on or something.

00:43:17.394 --> 00:43:19.797
Obviously there are black mambas
around here,

00:43:19.863 --> 00:43:21.699
but it's not that often
that they come inside.

00:43:21.765 --> 00:43:23.200
They're generally outside.

00:43:23.267 --> 00:43:24.601
But luckily you didn't
try to hit it,

00:43:24.668 --> 00:43:26.670
because that big snake like that
could probably bite you

00:43:26.737 --> 00:43:28.973
two or three times,
and then you're finished.

00:43:29.039 --> 00:43:30.874
And it's hospital, and if you
don't get to hospital quick,

00:43:30.941 --> 00:43:32.142
you're dead.

00:43:32.209 --> 00:43:34.912
Sometimes 10, 15 minutes.
It's enough.

00:43:34.979 --> 00:43:36.146
Very, very dangerous snake,
that one.

00:43:36.213 --> 00:43:37.381
SIOUXSIE: Yeah.

00:43:37.448 --> 00:43:39.216
SIMON: So, yeah, thanks for not
killing it either.

00:43:39.283 --> 00:43:40.484
We'll take it away,

00:43:40.551 --> 00:43:42.886
and we'll find it somewhere
where there's no people.

00:43:42.953 --> 00:43:43.988
Okay. Cool, man. Nice one.

00:43:44.054 --> 00:43:45.689
SIOUXSIE: Alright, cheers.
Thank you.

00:43:45.756 --> 00:43:47.358
SIMON: I'll take the box.

00:43:47.424 --> 00:43:49.259
Okay, set? Yeah, I will.

00:43:49.326 --> 00:43:50.427
Okay, let's go.

00:43:50.494 --> 00:43:51.595
SIOUXSIE: Thank you.

00:43:51.662 --> 00:43:53.397
SIMON: Thank you, guys.
SIOUXSIE: Bye! Bye!

00:43:53.464 --> 00:43:54.698
SIMON: Sorted.

00:43:54.765 --> 00:43:58.802
ALL: Bye!

00:43:58.869 --> 00:44:00.971
SIOUXSIE: Bye!

00:44:01.038 --> 00:44:02.172
MAN: Love you!

00:44:02.239 --> 00:44:04.308
[laughs]

00:44:04.375 --> 00:44:05.676
SIMON: It's a good feeling,
you know.

00:44:05.743 --> 00:44:07.544
Get the snake out of there,
the snake's fine,

00:44:07.611 --> 00:44:09.913
the people are fine,
we are all fine.

00:44:09.980 --> 00:44:11.515
And go home and sort
of just think about

00:44:11.582 --> 00:44:12.349
what you've just done.

00:44:12.416 --> 00:44:13.550
You know, it does sink in later.

00:44:13.617 --> 00:44:15.986
You think, Jesus,
that was dangerous.

00:44:16.053 --> 00:44:18.655
Well done.

00:44:18.722 --> 00:44:19.823
Okay, bye.

00:44:19.890 --> 00:44:20.991
Yeah, yeah.

00:44:21.058 --> 00:44:22.326
Cool, yeah.

00:44:22.393 --> 00:44:23.193
Okay, bye.

00:44:23.260 --> 00:44:24.695
KIDS: Bye!

